00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:13.519
Hi, welcome back to the lamrim. We're on episode 11. It's called Making it on the Tennis Team.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.080
And we're going to start out with a story from the lamrim about MCHOG ZUNG  and MCHOG means supreme

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.880
and ZUNG means

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:25.760
A pair of two people.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:31.039
And this is an important word in in secret practice and I can't tell you about it.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:34.559
But anyway MCHOG ZUNG means the big two.

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:38.960
And this refers to two of the most famous disciples of Lord Buddha,

00:00:39.840 --> 00:00:42.340
which are Shariputra and Maudgalyayana.

00:00:44.079 --> 00:00:48.479
We know Shariputra because he's the hero in the Heart Sutra.

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:52.960
He gets to ask a question and because of his question

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.479
we find we get the Heart Sutra. We get to hear the whole Heart Sutra.

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:01.839
The Buddha, it by the way, it is

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:03.840
traditionally

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.040
taught

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:07.359
that these two disciples of the Buddha became

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.080
arhats.  They reached nirvana.

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:16.579
But they reached it on a lower track. So they're in this category, both of them are in this category

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.759
of people who have reached a very high

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:22.640
personal space

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.640
where they are in complete bliss and they kind of

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.520
are are not so interested

00:01:30.159 --> 00:01:32.798
in the bodhisattva ideal of trying to

00:01:33.759 --> 00:01:35.680
meet every living being,

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:36.640
and

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.480
give this promise to them that, "I will take care of you." 

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:43.600
They traditionally, they're having too much bliss

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:48.239
in nirvana to to think about that much. So it happened one day

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:50.720
 that

00:01:50.720 --> 00:01:52.720
Lord Buddha

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.720
came to these two

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:58.239
and I don't know if he shook them awake or I don't know how he did it, but he,

00:01:58.880 --> 00:02:02.000
he said, "You know, I want to teach you guys about this higher thing

00:02:02.799 --> 00:02:08.719
where you take care of everybody and I want you to have this personal experience where you meet

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:14.319
every living being. I think it will change your life forever." So he encouraged them

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.080
and the reply by these two

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.640
arhats was,

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.640
NGO MTSAR, NGO MTSAR BA 'DUG KYANG 

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:24.640
NGO MTSAR  BA 'DUG KYANG 

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:28.400
In the second line here Seiji, probably. 

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.400
NGO MTSAR BA 'DUG KYANG 

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:33.620
"Wow that sounds amazing, you know, to meet every

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:37.200
single living being that, yeah, that would be something special."

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:38.540
KYANG, but,

00:02:38.780 --> 00:02:41.380
BDAG CAG NI SDONG DUM MES TSIG PA

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:42.680
BZHIN DU GYUR PAS

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:44.720
"Ever since we reached nirvana

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.720
we've been like a bump on a log."

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.000
It says here a tree trunk burned by

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:54.160
a,

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:56.160
an inert tree trunk

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.760
burned by fire or something like that.

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:02.319
But what it means is, "You know, we're just totally out of it

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.800
that sounds wonderful Buddha, but

00:03:05.519 --> 00:03:06.879
you know,

00:03:06.879 --> 00:03:09.679
don't teach this stuff to us. We're already in this kind of

00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:11.120
spaced out place

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.280
and we're going to be here for millions of years,

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:16.080
you know." So CI BYAR 

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:17.599
CI BYAR MI 'DUG 

00:03:17.599 --> 00:03:20.799
"We're not the people to be teaching this stuff to because we're already,

00:03:21.599 --> 00:03:23.926
we're already wrapped up in our personal nirvana.

00:03:23.926 --> 00:03:26.158
You're kind of wasting your time with us."

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.360
So there's this incident

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.400
where even this great

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.319
arhat who who requested the Heart Sutra,

00:03:37.040 --> 00:03:40.720
was staying in this kind of space and told Lord Buddha,

00:03:41.360 --> 00:03:43.360
"Maybe you shouldn't waste your time on us

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:45.120
because,

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.599
because we're in a bad,  we're in a good bad place

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.196
and we we can't really do it."

